      "shared_perspectives": "Across the political spectrum German media converge on the view that artificial‑intelligence systems pose concrete security and misuse risks, as illustrated by repeated reports of OpenAI‑related breaches, and therefore call for stronger oversight, liability rules and coordinated national implementation of the EU AI Act. At the same time there is a shared emphasis on the urgency of expanding digital infrastructure and building AI‑related skills, with frequent calls for faster broadband rollout, industry‑wide training programmes and education reforms to keep Germany competitive in Europe. Finally, coverage uniformly treats recent EU‑level regulatory moves, such as youth‑social‑media bans, as necessary but insufficient, urging German authorities to translate them into effective domestic policy.",
